From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 17:12:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: qcom: restore the VBUS override on resume too

The pipe-clk fix got the core initialising cleanly again -- the "failed
to enable ep0out" error is gone -- but the gadget still never appeared
on the bus. dwc3's own registers said why: DCTL = 0x80f00000, so
RUN_STOP was set and the controller was not halted, yet DSTS reported
link state Disconnected and the dwc3 interrupt advanced by exactly 1
across a whole suspend cycle. The controller was running and simply did
not believe a host was there.

Diffing QSCRATCH either side of one s2idle cycle names the two missing
bits:

    HS_PHY_CTRL 0x10100000 -> 0x10000000   UTMI_OTG_VBUS_VALID
    SS_PHY_CTRL 0x01000000 -> 0x00000000   LANE0_PWR_PRESENT

Both are the VBUS override that probe applies via
dwc3_qcom_vbus_override_enable() for peripheral mode. A board with no
VBUS sensing of its own relies on that override to tell the controller
it is plugged in. Losing it leaves the PHY with no reason to assert the
pullup, which is why the host saw nothing at all -- not a failed
enumeration, no bus activity whatsoever.

Re-apply it in resume alongside the pipe-clk selection, under the same
condition probe uses so no other mode's behaviour changes.

Verified on msm8998: after this, one s2idle cycle leaves GENERAL_CFG at
0x0d, HS_PHY_CTRL at 0x10100000, SS_PHY_CTRL at 0x01000000, link_state
"On", the dwc3 interrupt +112 instead of +1, and the USB gadget answers
on the other side of the suspend, over three consecutive cycles.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
index e957d5f016fc..7db6059cfd06 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -392,14 +392,17 @@ static int dwc3_qcom_resume(struct dwc3_qcom *qcom, bool wakeup)
 		dev_warn(qcom->dev, "failed to enable interconnect: %d\n", ret);
 
 	/*
-	 * QSCRATCH sits in the USB GDSC, which collapses while we are
-	 * suspended, so the probe-time pipe-clk selection does not survive.
-	 * Re-apply it here: this glue resumes before the core re-initialises,
-	 * so the core has a valid pipe clock by then.
+	 * Neither of the two things probe programs into QSCRATCH survives the
+	 * USB GDSC collapsing over suspend, so re-apply both. This glue
+	 * resumes before the core re-initialises, so they are back in place
+	 * by then.
 	 */
 	if (qcom->ignore_pipe_clk)
 		dwc3_qcom_select_utmi_clk(qcom);
 
+	if (qcom->mode == USB_DR_MODE_PERIPHERAL)
+		dwc3_qcom_vbus_override_enable(qcom, true);
+
 	/* Clear existing events from PHY related to L2 in/out */
 	for (i = 0; i < qcom->num_ports; i++) {
 		dwc3_qcom_setbits(qcom->qscratch_base,
